(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Janjati Adivasi Nyaya Maha Abhiyan (PM JANMAN) for the development of Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs);
(b) the key interventions in health, education, housing, connectivity and livelihood support provided to PVTG habitations; and
(c) the number of beneficiaries covered and infrastructure projects completed since the launch of the PM JANMAN scheme?

(a) the details of the guidelines used in selecting heavy industry clusters for deployment of carbon mitigation systems under the newly announced ?20,000 crore CCUS Technology Fund;
(b) whether Government has established a specific emissions-reduction audit framework to assess the efficiency of carbon capture in selected pilot thermal power plants;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government proposes to issue standardized rules to enable Municipal Corporations to issue green bonds for the rejuvenation of urban wetlands; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made in implementing Carbon Capture, Utilisation and Storage (CCUS) initiatives in the petroleum and natural gas sector; 
(b) the refineries and upstream projects identified for pilot implementation; 
(c) the incentives and regulatory framework proposed to encourage private investment in CCUS technologies; and 
(d) the contribution envisaged from CCUS towards achieving India's climate commitments?

(a) the progress made under the Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen Kaushalya Yojana (DDU-GKY) to align the skill development of rural youth with emerging employment opportunities and industry requirements, so far;
(b) the sectors, industries and emerging employment areas that have been identified for the training and placement of rural youth under the said scheme;
(c) the measures adopted by Government to ensure the placement of trained candidates, partnerships with industries and their post-placement retention; and
(d) the financial outlay proposed for the implementation of the Scheme, the details thereof?

(a) the current status and achievements of the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme for the Food Processing Industry;
(b) the details of the investment attracted, production achieved, and employment generated under the Scheme;
(c) the current status of the development and operationalization of Mega Food Parks along with the contribution made by these parks to the organized food processing sector; and
(d) the steps taken to promote the export of food products, strengthen the branding of Indian food products, and encourage the adoption of new technologies in the food processing industry?

(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana in creating modern food processing infrastructure and value addition facilities in all States including Maharashtra;
(b) the number of projects sanctioned, completed, and the employment generated through the scheme district-wise including Maharashtra;
(c) the steps taken to reduce post-harvest losses, promote farmer producer organisations, and enhance farmer income especially in the Khandesh and Marthwada rigion of Maharashtra; and
(d) the overall impact on food processing capacity, exports and growth of the sector?

(a) sector-wise and category-wise details of the total number of beneficiaries approved under the Production Linked Incentive scheme for Food Processing Industries (PLISFPI) since its launch;
(b) details of the cumulative investment made, production achieved and incentives disbursed under the scheme so far;
(c) details of the extent of participation of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs), cooperative institutions and innovative or organic product manufacturers under the scheme;
(d) whether any steps have been taken during the tenure of the scheme to enhance value addition, brand promotion and global competitiveness of Indian food products; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of the objectives and expected outcomes of the 'Mission for Atmanirbharta in Pulses' and 'Pradhan Mantri Dhan Dhaanya Krishi Yojana'; 
(b) the details of the financial allocation, duration and implementation period of both these schemes along with details of the targeted districts and hectare area; 
(c) the measures being adopted for coordination between States and nodal officers to ensure timebound and effective implementation; and
(d) the mechanisms in place under these initiatives to monitor progress, track benefits reaching farmers and to assess employment generation and improvement in productivity?

(a) whether Government has taken any initiative to promote the use of agro-textiles to enhance agricultural productivity and farmer welfare;
(b) if so, the details thereof including number, objectives, cost and operational status of the Smart Agro-Textile Centres established so far;
(c) the total number of farmers trained or benefited through such centres and programmes; and
(d) the plan of Government to expand agro-textile interventions in more areas of the country and to integrate them with rural livelihood schemes?

(a) the details of entities eligible for setting up, operating and maintaining electric vehicle (EV) charging stations under PM E-Drive scheme;
(b) the financial assistance and subsidy provisions including the total outlay for EV charging infrastructure proposed under the scheme;
(c) the criteria for selection of cities, towns and highways for installation of EV charging stations under the scheme including the focus on metropolitan cities, smart cities, satellite towns, State capitals; and
(d) the mechanisms and measures put in place to coordinate installation of EV charging stations and ensure effective deployment and maintenance of the infrastructure?

(a) the details of various courses conducted, admission procedures and activities offered at Lakshmibai National Institute of Physical Education (LNIPE);
(b) whether Government has taken any steps to promote sports education in the country and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of LNIPE centres established in Rajasthan to promote sports education there; and
(d) the funds released to LNIPE by Government during the last five years?

(a) the measures undertaken by Government to promote the country as a tourist destination;
(b) the initiatives taken to enhance visibility of domestic and overseas tourism;
(c) the steps being taken to promote MICE tourism and wedding tourism; and
(d) the manner in which citizen-engagement platforms are contributing to tourism awareness and destination discovery?

(a) the current status of fragrance and floriculture missions of CSIR;
(b) the extent to which these missions have been helpful in increasing the income of farmers;
(c) whether these missions have caused any significant impact on the Indian import/export market and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government is developing new varieties of flowers to empower farmers through floriculture and if so, the number of such varieties being developed?

(a) whether Government is running any special scheme for the relocation of villagers from protected forest areas; 
(b) if so, the financial assistance provided to State of Madhya Pradesh for this relocation; and 
(c) whether Government, keeping in view the need of additional assistance for the people relocated from the protected areas, proposes to provide central assistance or additional funds?

(a) whether Government has undertaken work related to safe drinking water, sewerage, urban transport and similar facilities in 32 cities of the State of Madhya Pradesh under the AMRUT Scheme; 
(b) the number of urban local bodies where work is in progress under AMRUT 2.0; and
(c) the sectors in which the State attained key achievements under the AMRUT Scheme?

(a) whether an irrigated area of 5 lakh hectares has been developed across 10 projects in the State of Madhya Pradesh under the Accelerated Irrigation Benefit Program of the Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana;
(b) by when the approval would be accorded, which has been submitted to Government, with regard to the inclusion of Sanjay Sarovar Irrigation Project (Seoni/Balaghat) in the scheme; and 
(c) the total funds received by the State so far under the AIBP scheme?

(a) whether a proposal has been sent to the Government of India for the establishment of National Institute of Food Technology Entrepreneurship and Management (NIFTEM) in Madhya Pradesh;
(b) if so, the current status of the establishment of this institute and the action which has been taken so far for its approval;
(c) whether the approval of ?15 crore for MIDH (Export Oriented Centre of Excellence) project for mango/vegetable in Harda district is pending; and
(d) if so, the current status of the approval of the said project and the steps taken to remove the obstacles in its implementation?

(a) the total number of reported human-wildlife incidents across the country after 2020, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the details of provision of providing payment of compensation to the victims in case of human-wildlife conflict;
(c) the eligibility, amount and payment process of compensation; 
(d) whether Government is considering to enhance the compensation amount in light of rising incidents and demands from States; and
(e) if so, the amount distributed as compensation in the last five years, year-wise and State-wise?

(a) whether Government has implemented any special scheme to promote tree plantation (development of private forests) in the private sector;
(b) if so, the amount of financial assistance provided so far to the State of Madhya Pradesh under this scheme; and
(c) if not, by when Government is planning to launch any special initiative or scheme in this direction?

(a) the objectives and significance of establishing five Carbon Capture and Utilisation (CCU) testbeds in the cement sector and how this initiative supports India’s net-zero target by 2070;
(b) the institutions and industry partners involved in the CCU testbeds and the distinct technological solutions being developed at each site; and
(c) the expected impact of these CCU testbeds on CO2 reduction in the cement industry and their potential for scaling to other hard-to-abate sectors?

(a) the steps taken to increase awareness among small and marginal farmers about subsidy available for storage facilities;
(b) whether the Ministry is planning to increase the upper limit of ?1.75 lakh so that increased cost of onion storage facilities construction can be adjusted;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether the Ministry is planning to cover more perishable crops under the scheme in future; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether it is a fact that Council of Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR) has developed e-tractor; 
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and 
(c) if so, the details of other tractors developed by CSIR?

(a) whether it is a fact that Council of Scientific and Industrial Research has developed a technology for converting biomedical waste into soil additives; 
(b) if so, the details thereof and the current status of technology transfer; and 
(c) the manner in which this technology can be leveraged to effectively address issues in the management of biomedical waste?

(a) the details of the implementation and adoption status of the e-GramSwaraj initiative, launched in April 2020 to improve the functioning of Panchayats; 
(b) the number of Gram Panchayats that have uploaded their Gram Panchayat Development Plans (GPDPs) on the e-GramSwaraj platform for the financial year 2023-24; 
(c) the percentage of the total Gram Panchayats that are currently using the e-GramSwaraj platform in the country, along with the measures being taken by the Ministry to promote its adoption among the remaining panchayats; and 
(d) whether any future reforms or additional features are planned to further strengthen the functionality of Panchayats improve governance for the e-Gram Swaraj platform?

(a) whether there is any plan to expand M-PACS model further; 
(b) if so, the details thereof; 
(c) the number of farmers, dairy producers and fisherman expected to directly benefit from these newly established cooperative societies; and 
(d) the manner in which this initiative would be linked to the broader goals of rural development?
