(a) the expected timeline for the establishment of the All India Institute of Ayurveda and 11 other Ayurveda colleges;
(b) the primary research areas that would be explored by the All India Institute of Ayurveda;
(c) the manner in which this Institute would contribute to the development of Ayurveda in India and globally; and
(d) whether this Institute would collaborate with international Ayurveda or Organizations for alternative medicine?

(a) the number of cities expected to participate in this edition of Swachh Sarvekshan ;
(b) whether any efforts are being made to ensure wider participation across all urban areas;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether any new technologies or methodologies have been introduced to measure cleanliness and hygiene; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Ministry has taken steps to reduce the number of blind spots present on roads for ensuring road safety of citizens;
(b) if so, the details of total number of blind spots identified by the Ministry; and
(c) the importance of road safety measures and focus of the Ministry to build good quality roads?

(a) the measures taken by Government to push ethanol blending with petrol;
(b) whether ethanol blending contributes towards reducing dependence on imported oil and addressing environmental concerns; and
(c) the total surge in ethanol-blended petrol supply during the last five years?

(a) whether the Ministry has set a target to establish sustainable cooperative societies such as dairy and fisheries cooperative societies, in Panchayats, if so, the details thereof, State-wise including the State of Uttarakhand;
(b) the details of the schemes through which the Ministry has digitized the Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) by connecting them to ERP based software; and
(c) the details of the total number of PACS on ERP based software till date?
